.TH ZERODDS-CORBA-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-corba-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-corba-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/corba-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the CORBA bridge daemon maps CORBA interface
operations onto DDS topics. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-corba-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/corba-dds-bridge/src/bridge_daemon.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " corba ", " acl ", " mappings ", " metrics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr naming the key, then
starts; under
.B \-\-check\-config
it is an error. An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the
wrong type, stops the start with file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed. A
.B #
inside a quoted value is part of the value, not the start of a comment \(em a
.I corbaname
URL depends on that.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS corba
.TP
.B orb_id
ORB identifier of this daemon.
.TP
.B iiop
Sub-map with
.B bind
(listen address, e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:6833" ,
the default),
.B advertise_host
(the host the IORs name when
.B bind
is a wildcard address; default
.IR 127.0.0.1 ,
environment
.BR ZERODDS_CORBA_ADVERTISE_HOST ),
.B giop_version
.RI ( 1.0 " | " 1.1 " | " 1.2 ;
a mapped operation reached over 1.0 or 1.1 is answered NO_IMPLEMENT),
.B fragment_size
(replies above it go out in GIOP 1.2 fragments) and
.B max_message_size
(a larger inbound message is answered MessageError).
.TP
.B ssliop
Sub-map with
.BR enabled ", " bind ,
the server material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file ,
.B ca_file
and
.B require_client_cert
(the client certificate is checked against
.BR ca_file ;
its subject DN, RFC 4514, is the ACL subject).
.TP
.B ior
Sub-map with
.B ior_file
(one line per mapping:
.IR "repo_id operation IOR:..." ),
.B naming_service
(a
.IR corbaname: " or " corbaloc:
URL, CORBA 3.4 Part 2 \(sc13.6.10; only an
.I iiop:
or protocol-less endpoint is resolved \(em
.IR rir: " and " ssliop:/tls:
naming-service connections are refused by name, not attempted),
.B publish_to_naming
(boolean: rebinds every receiving mapping's IOR into
.B naming_service
at start, under
.I <corbaname-fragment-path>/<repo_id-operation slug>
\(em every missing intermediate context in the path is created;
.I unbind
at a clean stop; requires
.BR naming_service )
and
.B naming_retry_ms
(total retry budget against
.BR naming_service ,
exponential backoff from 200\ ms capped at 5\ s; default
.IR 30000 ,
matching this daemon's own shutdown drain and its packaged unit's
.BR TimeoutStopSec ).
.TP
.B naming
Sub-map with
.B serve
(host a
.I zerodds-corba-cosnaming
NamingContext, object key
.IR NameService ,
on this daemon's own IIOP/SSLIOP listener \(em not built).
.TP
.B csiv2
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean: every request's SAS
.I EstablishContext
is evaluated; a rejected one is
.B NO_PERMISSION
with a SAS
.B ContextError
attached; additive next to SSLIOP client certificates and the ACL \(em
this daemon has both, unlike
.BR zerodds-naming-svc (1)),
.B target_supports
(list of accepted
.I IdentityToken
forms for CSIv2 identity assertion, Spec \(sc24.2.5: any of
.IR anonymous ", " principal_name ", " x509_cert_chain ", " distinguished_name ;
an asserted identity of an unlisted form is refused) and
.BR gssup ,
a sub-map with
.B password_file
(a GSSUP credential file:
.I username:salt_hex:iterations:hash_hex
per line, PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 \(em no plain-text password anywhere in this
daemon's configuration; required when
.B enabled
is true) and
.B target_name
(the AS-context target name this daemon's
.B TAG_CSI_SEC_MECH_LIST
IOR component advertises).
A CSIv2-accepted identity is added to the ACL's subjects as
.IR gssup:<username> ,
or, for an accepted identity assertion, the asserted name verbatim.
.SS acl
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean: without a rule for the caller, NO_PERMISSION.
.TP
.B rules
List of maps with
.B subject
.RI ( * ,
the client certificate's subject DN such as
.IR CN=trader,O=Example ,
or its fingerprint
.IR mtls:<SHA-256 hex> )
and
.BR allow_invoke ,
repository ids, a trailing
.I *
matching a prefix.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9096"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
.TP
.B path
Only
.IR /metrics .
.SS mappings (list)
Each entry binds one CORBA operation to DDS topics.
.TP
.B repo_id
CORBA repository ID of the interface, e.g.
.IR "IDL:fin/PortfolioPublisher:1.0" .
.TP
.B operation
Operation name on that interface.
.TP
.B direction
.IR corba_to_dds " | " dds_to_corba " | " bidir .
.TP
.B request_topic
Sub-map carrying
.B dds_name
and
.BR dds_type ;
by default derived from repo_id and operation (\(sc5.1).
.TP
.B reply_topic
Sub-map as request_topic.
.TP
.B notify_topic
Sub-map as request_topic, for dds_to_corba.
.TP
.B correlation_id
Only
.IR request_id ,
the first member of the request and reply types.
.TP
.B timeout_ms
Reply wait; without a reply by then the caller gets TIMEOUT.
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ;
request-reply needs reliable) and
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local ).
.TP
.B targets
For dds_to_corba: corbaloc URLs or stringified IORs every notify sample is
sent to as a oneway request.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/corba-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged (1).
